-- title:
--   Inertia-fixed elements have valuation a power of varpi
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field equipped with an algebra structure over which $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (realised as `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) is an extension, let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $q$ be a prime such that `P.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the non-units of $P$. Let $\varpi \in F$ have image in $P$, and assume that $\varpi$, viewed as an element of the valuation subring $P$ pulled back to $F$ along the structure map, is irreducible there. Let $M$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/F$ which is finite-dimensional and Galois over $F$, and let $Q$ be a maximal ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_M$ which is described by the two valuation conditions: every element of $\mathcal{O}_M$ has $P$-valuation at most $1$, and an element of $\mathcal{O}_M$ lies in $Q$ exactly when its $P$-valuation is strictly less than $1$. Finally let $y \in M$ be nonzero and fixed by every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup `Q.inertia` of $\mathrm{Gal}(M/F)$. The conclusion is that there is an integer $n$ with $P.\mathrm{valuation}\big(y \cdot \varpi^{\,n}\big) = 1$, that is, the $P$-valuation of $y$ is an integral power of that of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the statement that the inertia field inside a finite Galois layer $M/F$ is unramified at the place induced by $P$, in the form needed for valuations on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the valuation of an inertia-fixed element is generated by the valuation of a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $F$ at that place. It is used, together with the computation of the ramification indices of $Q$ over the fixed field of its inertia subgroup and the reading of $P$-valuations off $Q$-adic orders, by [`ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_comap_fixedField_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_irreducible`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_comap_fixedField_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_irreducible) to exhibit the relevant pulled-back valuation ring as a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_valuation_mul_zpow_eq_one_of_forall_inertia_apply_eq.lean

